  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Let $a\\geq0$ and $m,n\\in\\mathbb{N}$. Prove that $\\sqrt[m]{a^n}=(\\sqrt[m]{a})^n$. Hint: evaluate $((\\sqrt[m]{a})^n)^m$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sqrt[m]{a^n}=(\\sqrt[m]{a})^n$.\n\nRaise $(\\sqrt[m]{a})^n$ to the power $m$, then take the nonnegative $m$th root.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\bigl((\\sqrt[m]{a})^n\\bigr)^m&=(\\sqrt[m]{a})^{nm}\\\\\\bigl((\\sqrt[m]{a})^n\\bigr)^m&=\\bigl((\\sqrt[m]{a})^m\\bigr)^n\\\\\\bigl((\\sqrt[m]{a})^n\\bigr)^m&=a^n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $(\\sqrt[m]{a})^n\\geq0$, taking the nonnegative $m$th root gives\n$$\\sqrt[m]{a^n}=(\\sqrt[m]{a})^n.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
